1
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:11,520
But if you ever hurt Papang
like this again,

2
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:13,000
I won't let it go.

3
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:15,320
When I hate someone,

4
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:17,080
I hate them until the day I die.

5
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:21,920
I told you. I'm Ramil's wife.

6
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,040
PREVIOUSLY

7
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,880
How about I take you to your parents?

8
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:27,920
I'll help you out.

9
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:37,960
Papang.

10
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:40,760
Daddy's going to work now. Bye.

11
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,680
-Be a good boy.
-Bye.

12
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:44,920
-Let's go.
-Alright.

13
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,880
Papang.

14
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:50,680
Mommy brought your game.

15
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:51,600
Come on.

16
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,000
-What are you doing?
-Well…

17
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,440
Did you change your mind?

18
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,120
I'm going with you.

19
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,520
What are you going to do?

20
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:01,960
Want to go home instead?
I can drop you off.

21
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:04,920
I'm going with you.

22
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,280
I'm going to work.

23
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:09,400
My son and I
won't interfere with your work.

24
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:11,560
The development is huge.

25
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:14,000
I also want to pay my respects
to Mr. Pichai.

26
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:17,040
Papang, do you miss Great-Grandpa Pichai?

27
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:19,600
Yes. He's very kind.

28
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:23,240
Let's go. I don't want
to make you late for work.

29
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:26,080
Hathaya.

30
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:30,520
Carry that basket and bring
those things over there too.

31
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:37,840
Can't do it? If you can't, Papang
and I can carry them ourselves.

32
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,400
It's okay. I'll carry them.

33
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,560
Let's go, Daddy.

34
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,040
Come on.

35
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,400
Let's get in the car.

36
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:57,440
Hey,

37
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,960
take Papang to my office first.
I need to check on the workers.

38
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,840
Everyone, come over here, please.

39
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:12,040
Hathaya, bring the basket here.

40
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,800
I made sandwiches for everyone.

41
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,480
Boss, your friend is really nice.

42
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,960
I'm not his friend.

43
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:30,160
My name is Nuchwara. I'm Papang's mother

44
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:33,400
and your boss's wife.

45
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:37,520
Everyone, get back to work.

46
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:38,480
Go.

47
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:45,960
Papang.

48
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,480
-Daddy has to work now.
-Okay.

49
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,520
Be good, all right?

50
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:51,480
Give Daddy a kiss.

51
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:05,920
I'm going to get to work too.

52
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,360
Carry the basket and follow me.

53
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,880
And get the things from the trunk too.

54
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,520
Hello, Grandpa.

55
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,240
-Hello, Great-Grandpa.
-Hello.

56
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:22,480
Hello.

57
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:25,600
-Hello, Great-Grandpa.
-Hello, my dear.

58
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,760
Hello.

59
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:31,040
I haven't seen you in a long time.
You've grown so much.

60
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,320
Are you doing well?

61
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,120
I want you to stay strong.

62
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,720
Why is that?

63
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:40,800
So you can carry me
around the whole development.

64
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,800
I'm too old for that now.

65
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:45,760
But I have a golf cart.
Want me to drive you around in that?

66
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:49,080
-Yes. Let's go.
-Okay.

67
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:52,080
Hathaya, give me the basket.

68
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,640
Let's go.

69
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:04,080
Grandpa,

70
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:08,440
I brought you sandwiches,
chicken salad, and fresh orange juice.

71
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:10,040
Thank you.

72
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,880
I just felt like having that.

73
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:14,960
Can I take a picture with you?
I've missed you.

74
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,880
-Take our picture.
-Come on.

75
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,360
Let's take a picture.

76
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:39,200
One, two, three.

77
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,000
Good.

78
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:46,520
-How have you been, Grandpa?
-I've been well.

79
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,880
Then…

80
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:50,040
I'll get back to work.

81
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:53,760
Come on. Let's go for a ride.

82
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:55,320
Let's go.

83
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:57,920
Let's go have some fun.

84
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,480
I really have to thank you both

85
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,800
for being so generous.

86
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:09,560
Look at my crew.

87
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,640
They're working day and night

88
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,280
without getting tired.

89
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,520
That's the power of overtime pay.

90
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:17,800
At this rate,
the work will be finished quickly.

91
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:21,000
Don't let what happened
yesterday happen again.

92
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:23,240
If the houses aren't finished
by the contract date,

93
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:25,320
I'll have to pay a fortune in penalties.

94
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:27,920
Don't worry, madam.

95
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,840
You can trust me.

96
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,880
I won't disappoint you or Miss Chayanee.

97
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:35,400
Money really is wonderful.

98
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:36,520
It can buy almost anything.

99
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,240
But believe it or not, miss,

100
00:08:38,919 --> 00:08:39,919
money can't buy me.

101
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:42,159
For me,

102
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:46,160
it's all heart.
Give me yours, and I'll give you mine.

103
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:52,600
You and Madam treat me this well,

104
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:53,960
and I'll work my hardest for you.

105
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,800
Come on. Faster.

106
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:03,200
-Keep working hard.
-Madam. Madam.

107
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,240
Miss Chayanee.

108
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,600
What is it, Chamoi? What's wrong with you?

109
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,800
What is it now?

110
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:12,960
I just wanted Madam and Miss Chayanee

111
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,680
to have a good laugh too.

112
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:18,360
Have you lost your mind?

113
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:20,640
What are you laughing at?

114
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,120
Hathaya

115
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,840
has officially been pushed aside.

116
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:31,200
Madam, Ramil's real wife is here.

117
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,120
She's been going around telling everyone

118
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:35,600
she's Ramil's wife.

119
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,600
I completely forgot

120
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:42,240
Ramil already had a wife.

121
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:45,640
Well, this is going to expose
that whole fake marriage, isn't it?

122
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:47,960
Wait. Where are you going?

123
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,240
I'm going to work.

124
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:54,240
You don't look fit to work at all.

125
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:58,320
Maybe you should see a veterinarian.

126
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:02,000
Madam?

127
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:05,120
Why would she need a veterinarian?

128
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:08,360
Because she's a sick dog
nobody wants anymore.

129
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:10,360
She needs treatment.

130
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,160
Mom.

131
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:15,680
A veterinarian

132
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:18,360
can't treat that.

133
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:19,640
You'd have to cremate it.

134
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:25,760
Where are you rushing off to?

135
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,160
The temple.

136
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:31,400
Going to have yourself cremated?

137
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,640
I'm going to make merit.

138
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:40,120
I thought I'd dedicate some merit
to wicked spirits.

139
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:43,480
Madam,

140
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:45,920
she was trying to insult you.

141
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:50,800
I know. She's the one
who's going to die of a broken heart

142
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:52,880
and become a wicked spirit.

143
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,040
Exactly.

144
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:59,120
Papang, be good for Great-Grandpa.

145
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,080
P.C. PROPERTY

146
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,160
It's been a long time. How have you been?

147
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:10,160
If I weren't doing well,
I probably wouldn't be standing here.

148
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,760
Is that how friends greet each other?

149
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,680
Did you ever consider me a friend?

150
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:25,000
I forgot. We were just people
who happened to be in the same class.

151
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:26,520
Not friends.

152
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:28,840
Are you still angry with me

153
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:33,640
because I liked Raiwin,
the same man you liked?

154
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:36,480
Why would I be angry?

155
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Raiwin wasn't interested in you,
so you went back to Ramil.

156
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:41,400
You really are something.

157
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:43,880
You only go after rich men's sons.

158
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:47,240
Then you got yourself pregnant
and had to drop out of college.

159
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:49,120
But the pathetic part is that in the end,

160
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:52,480
all you got was a useless stepson
who'll never amount to anything.

161
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,120
What are you laughing at?

162
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:05,040
If you knew the truth,

163
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:07,800
you'd probably cry your eyes out.

164
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:10,520
What are you talking about?

165
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:14,960
Chayanee is so smart.

166
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,400
Good at everything.

167
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,680
If you want to know,
investigate it yourself.

168
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:22,200
If I told you,

169
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:24,240
you might go into shock.

170
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:27,160
Take care of yourself.

171
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,520
Because

172
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,440
I've moved into Ramil's house now.

173
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,800
Let's see who survives this.

174
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:42,520
You're Chayanee's mother, right?

175
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,160
Yes.

176
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:47,920
I hope you don't mind
if I don't greet you properly.

177
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:51,040
I'm not Chayanee's friend.

178
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:56,320
But I do have one thing to tell you.
When you have time,

179
00:12:56,400 --> 00:13:00,400
take your daughter to wash her mouth out.
It's incredibly filthy.

180
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,560
That was harsh.

181
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:04,840
Really harsh.

182
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:08,520
Who is that foul-mouthed woman?

183
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:21,120
She was someone I knew in college.

184
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,360
She used to chase Raiwin,

185
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:26,160
but he wasn't interested in her.

186
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:29,160
Then she got pregnant and dropped out.

187
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:32,200
Ramil claimed the baby as his,

188
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:35,960
but they lived separately. Ramil would
only visit the child once in a while.

189
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,400
Now I remember.

190
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:42,240
She brought that child here
to play with Father before.

191
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:44,640
She has a vicious mouth.

192
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:47,880
Miss Chayanee, you need
to get rid of her and send her far away.

193
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:53,920
If you knew the truth,

194
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,680
you'd probably cry your eyes out.

195
00:13:57,600 --> 00:14:00,360
If you want to know,
investigate it yourself.

196
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:05,040
If I told you, you might go into shock.

197
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:07,440
The way she threatened me just now…

198
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:10,720
It sounded like
there's some secret I don't know.

199
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:13,400
Don't pay any attention to her.

200
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:16,360
Actually, I think it's good
that she came back to Ramil.

201
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:19,240
How is that good, madam?

202
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:27,120
She can get rid of Hathaya for us.

203
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,240
Then we won't have to waste
our own energy.

204
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:31,720
Let those two women tear each other apart.

205
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:39,600
Hathaya will get pressured
from every direction

206
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:44,240
until she can't take it anymore and runs
back to the countryside on her own.

207
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:55,360
Sir, I'm sorry

208
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:59,040
that Nuchwara and Papang
came to work like this.

209
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:03,520
I thought you and Nuchwara

210
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:05,640
were separated and had no obligations.

211
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,200
That's why I allowed Hathaya
to stay with you.

212
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,080
So how did this happen?

213
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:14,840
I didn't expect Nuchwara

214
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:17,320
to bring Papang and move in either.

215
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,960
You know why

216
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,160
I agreed to claim Papang as my son.

217
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:25,160
I know how much you sacrificed.

218
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:27,760
But now you're not alone anymore.

219
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:30,600
Hathaya is living with you too.

220
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:35,480
No matter how much you insist,

221
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,280
there's nothing between the two of you,

222
00:15:39,280 --> 00:15:43,120
everyone else believes
you're husband and wife.

223
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:47,120
I want you to take responsibility
for Hathaya's feelings too.

224
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:49,760
Yes, sir.

225
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:51,240
Papang.

226
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:53,200
Come on.

227
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:57,360
I will take you to see
the pond in the development.

228
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,480
-Want to go?
-Yes.

229
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:01,560
Come on. Take this with you too.

230
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,000
Let's go.

231
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:28,400
Hathaya.

232
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:31,800
How are you doing?

233
00:16:32,560 --> 00:16:34,480
I'm okay.

234
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:38,960
Has Nuchwara bothered you again?

235
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:43,640
If she said or did
anything inappropriate, I'm sorry.

236
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:48,160
I already told you.
No matter what happens, I'm on your side.

237
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:55,760
It's lunchtime. Come eat with me.

238
00:16:58,560 --> 00:16:59,400
Let's go.

239
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,480
Ramil.

240
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:05,640
I brought lunch for you.

241
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:13,920
Thanks. But you go ahead and eat first.

242
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:16,960
Come eat with us. Your son is waiting.

243
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:26,160
Hathaya, come eat with us.

244
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,720
I brought enough for you too.

245
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:31,760
Come on.

246
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:33,920
Come on.

247
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:54,000
-Come on, Hathaya. Eat with us.
-I made your favorite too.

248
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,560
Hathaya.

249
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:07,040
Could you feed Papang for me?

250
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:14,000
Papang, let Aunt Hathaya feed you.

251
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:21,400
You eat first.

252
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:22,800
No. I'll feed you.

253
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:24,360
-Come on. It's good.
-I'll do it.

254
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:26,680
I want to feed you.

255
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:38,240
Is it good?

256
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,240
Hathaya.

257
00:18:49,320 --> 00:18:51,000
Wash the food containers

258
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:52,840
and the other things for me.

259
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:54,800
Okay.

260
00:18:56,640 --> 00:18:58,640
And give Papang a bath too.

261
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,120
He's all sweaty and sticky.

262
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:02,120
Why don't you bathe your own son?

263
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:05,760
I just got back from work. I'm tired.

264
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:10,360
I'll bathe him.

265
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,280
Go.

266
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:19,400
Come on, Papang. Come with me.

267
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:22,280
You've been working so hard.

268
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,680
Come sit over here.

269
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:26,080
Come on.

270
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:31,280
I'll give you a massage.

271
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:36,400
Your shoulders look tense.

272
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:39,040
You must be stressed.

273
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,120
What should I do about that?

274
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:50,680
Papang, we're out of soap.

275
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,240
I'll run downstairs and get some.

276
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:59,440
You hardly look any different
from when we were in college.

277
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:02,240
But I like you better now.

278
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,240
You're more attractive.

279
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:08,760
What are you doing?

280
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:10,840
I'm going

281
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:14,240
to take off your shirt
so you can cool down.

282
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:16,960
Then I'll massage you.

283
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,440
No.

284
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:21,520
Come on. Don't upset your wife.

285
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:23,400
That's enough.

286
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:25,360
Let go.

287
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:31,680
I regret ever being obsessed
with your brother.

288
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:34,040
If I could go back,

289
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:36,080
I would choose you instead.

290
00:20:37,680 --> 00:20:40,080
I think I would've been much happier.

291
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,520
But it doesn't matter now.

292
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:48,080
Because the two of us are a family anyway.

293
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,440
You're my husband.

294
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:54,680
Stop fantasizing.
You know none of this is real.

295
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:58,200
Then I'll make it real.

296
00:20:58,720 --> 00:20:59,720
Get off me.

297
00:21:01,520 --> 00:21:03,360
Why do you have to treat me like this?

298
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,920
I have to lie to everyone

299
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:08,040
and say you're my wife.

300
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:14,280
But I can't lie to myself.
I have never loved you.

301
00:21:14,360 --> 00:21:15,680
And I never will.

302
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:19,040
Then can't you open your heart to me?

303
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:23,000
I want us to be a real family

304
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,200
for our son.

305
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:29,360
Stop using Papang as an excuse.
What you're doing

306
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:32,680
is offering yourself up
to get what you want.

307
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:35,960
Stop clinging to rich men
like you always have.

308
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:47,120
Then what am I supposed to do?

309
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:51,840
How am I ever supposed to have
a comfortable life like everyone else?

310
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:54,840
First,

311
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:58,120
stop comparing your life
to everyone else's.

312
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:00,840
If you want a comfortable life,

313
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:05,560
you have to build it yourself.
Stop looking for a shortcut.

314
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:09,920
And all this time,

315
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:13,000
I've constantly helped you
solve your problems.

316
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:14,880
You should have learned from it

317
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:16,880
and changed yourself.

318
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,120
Listen to me.

319
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:23,360
You can't depend on me
for the rest of your life.

320
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:27,480
One day, I'm going to have my own life.
My own family.

321
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:27,800
Where are Nuchwara and Papang?

322
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:31,400
I haven't seen Nuchwara
come out of her room yet.

323
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:32,960
She must be really upset.

324
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:39,320
I had to say those things.

325
00:23:40,800 --> 00:23:42,440
I've helped her enough.

326
00:23:43,240 --> 00:23:45,280
She has to start solving her own problems.

327
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:52,040
If this had been before,

328
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:54,960
I probably would've thought
you were cruel.

329
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:58,280
But now that I know the whole story,

330
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:00,760
I understand.

331
00:24:08,320 --> 00:24:09,600
I love Papang.

332
00:24:12,040 --> 00:24:14,320
And I care deeply about his feelings.

333
00:24:17,960 --> 00:24:20,120
When the time is right,

334
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:23,280
I think we should tell Papang the truth.

335
00:24:24,520 --> 00:24:27,120
He has a right to know his own story.

336
00:24:33,520 --> 00:24:34,360
Papang.

337
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:36,760
Come on. Let's eat.

338
00:24:37,560 --> 00:24:38,960
I'm taking Papang away.

339
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:42,600
-Where?
-Back to my house.

340
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:47,720
Hey, Hathaya.

341
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:52,120
If you're willing to help,

342
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:55,160
carry the bags and take Papang to the car.

343
00:24:55,760 --> 00:24:56,920
-Okay.
-I'll do it.

344
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:05,440
Papang, come eat first. Come with me.

345
00:25:08,040 --> 00:25:09,040
Are you hungry?

346
00:25:18,440 --> 00:25:20,120
You're heartless.

347
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:22,320
You're not even going to ask me to stay?

348
00:25:23,840 --> 00:25:25,160
Just because I don't stop you

349
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:27,400
doesn't mean I don't care about Papang.

350
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:29,880
I just think this is the best solution.

351
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:31,760
Just because I'm leaving

352
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:34,600
doesn't mean I agree with you.

353
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:40,800
People aren't born
with the same advantages.

354
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:42,840
You expect me to start over now?

355
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:44,280
It's too late.

356
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:48,680
Hard work is for diligent people.

357
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:52,320
Shortcuts are for smart people.

358
00:25:56,400 --> 00:25:57,360
Whatever you say.

359
00:26:01,680 --> 00:26:02,800
Oh.

360
00:26:09,040 --> 00:26:12,360
I don't want to go.
I'm going to miss you, Daddy.

361
00:26:13,920 --> 00:26:16,880
Come on. Daddy will miss you too.

362
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:18,040
How about this?

363
00:26:18,120 --> 00:26:19,800
Daddy will video call you every day.

364
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:21,880
Promise?

365
00:26:22,480 --> 00:26:23,280
I promise.

366
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,160
Good boy.

367
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:34,160
Take care. We'll see each other soon.

368
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:36,600
Are you going to miss me too?

369
00:26:36,680 --> 00:26:38,200
Of course.

370
00:26:38,280 --> 00:26:40,880
I'll be so lonely without you around.

371
00:26:41,560 --> 00:26:42,640
No one left to argue with.

372
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:47,840
When I come back,
I'll argue with you again.

373
00:27:02,720 --> 00:27:05,920
Just because I'm leaving
doesn't mean I'm giving up.

374
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,880
I'll be back.

375
00:27:39,840 --> 00:27:40,800
Hey.

376
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:46,840
Is something wrong?

377
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:48,640
You've barely spoken since we left home.

378
00:27:49,640 --> 00:27:50,760
No.

379
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:54,160
If something is wrong, you can tell me.

380
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:57,760
I'm going to work.

381
00:28:11,280 --> 00:28:12,680
Where did all the workers go?

382
00:28:13,640 --> 00:28:16,240
Pong, where are your workers?

383
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:17,600
Why aren't they here?

384
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:19,560
I've been calling them,

385
00:28:20,080 --> 00:28:22,800
but the other contractor
sent pickups to pick them up.

386
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:24,480
What is that supposed to mean?

387
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:27,920
It means the other site is paying more,

388
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:29,640
so they all went over there.

389
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:31,760
I'm already paying them plenty.

390
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:33,800
What else do they want?
I'm not paying more.

391
00:28:34,520 --> 00:28:36,680
Pong, you're responsible for this.

392
00:28:37,280 --> 00:28:38,680
Madam,

393
00:28:38,760 --> 00:28:40,960
I already called them.

394
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:42,920
I called other contractors too,

395
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:44,920
but nobody is available.

396
00:28:46,360 --> 00:28:48,200
How about

397
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:51,800
we try another approach?

398
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:53,240
What approach?

399
00:28:54,280 --> 00:28:56,480
Could you add

400
00:28:57,360 --> 00:28:59,000
another 50 baht?

401
00:28:59,080 --> 00:29:01,120
I'll tell them.
I'm sure they'll come back--

402
00:29:01,200 --> 00:29:02,560
I'm not paying any more.

403
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:04,920
Mom.

404
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:08,640
Pong has caused damage to the project.

405
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:11,160
Fire him and find another crew.

406
00:29:13,520 --> 00:29:16,280
Calm down. It isn't fair to blame Pong.

407
00:29:16,360 --> 00:29:18,720
Those workers are the ones
who abandoned the job.

408
00:29:19,480 --> 00:29:21,360
But Pong is the foreman.

409
00:29:22,160 --> 00:29:23,720
He has to take responsibility.

410
00:29:25,520 --> 00:29:26,360
Pong,

411
00:29:26,440 --> 00:29:29,440
go get those workers back here.

412
00:29:29,520 --> 00:29:31,240
Before Father finds out.

413
00:29:32,560 --> 00:29:33,600
Yes, madam.

414
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:35,480
Come on. Let's go back to the office

415
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:36,840
before he inspects the site.

416
00:29:36,920 --> 00:29:38,120
Madam.

417
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:40,160
What? I'm in a hurry.

418
00:29:40,240 --> 00:29:41,280
Well…

419
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:42,560
Move.

420
00:29:46,080 --> 00:29:47,280
Where did all the workers go?

421
00:29:50,960 --> 00:29:53,880
Father, I'm sorry.

422
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:56,320
There was a small accident.

423
00:29:56,880 --> 00:30:00,040
The workers' vehicle broke down,
so they couldn't come in today.

424
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:01,280
Their vehicle broke down?

425
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:04,600
-Yes.
-Or did they abandon this job?

426
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:10,720
I noticed no one was working here,

427
00:30:10,800 --> 00:30:13,000
so I asked some workers I know.

428
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:16,800
They said the foreman here

429
00:30:16,880 --> 00:30:20,440
told the crew to stop working
and go work on another project.

430
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:23,760
I want to know who gave that order.

431
00:30:29,120 --> 00:30:30,600
It wasn't me, sir.

432
00:30:31,120 --> 00:30:33,880
You know how much effort
I put into this place.

433
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:37,120
The contractor they're talking about

434
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:39,400
must be an old contractor.

435
00:30:39,480 --> 00:30:41,040
He's notorious for abandoning jobs.

436
00:30:41,120 --> 00:30:44,320
If you knew the old contractor
was unreliable,

437
00:30:44,400 --> 00:30:46,600
why did you bring him onto my project?

438
00:30:50,360 --> 00:30:51,440
Father,

439
00:30:51,520 --> 00:30:54,280
you can't really blame Pong.

440
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:58,120
Another development
was probably jealous of ours

441
00:30:58,200 --> 00:31:01,520
and deliberately offered our workers
more money to steal them away.

442
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:05,200
Stop blaming other people.

443
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:09,120
You were the one who brought Pong to me

444
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:12,000
and guaranteed that he
was such a professional.

445
00:31:12,520 --> 00:31:14,520
A real professional
doesn't operate like this.

446
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:21,520
-Ramil.
-Yes, sir.

447
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:25,000
From now, you're responsible
for overseeing all the work here.

448
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:27,040
Of course, sir.

449
00:31:27,120 --> 00:31:29,440
Father, what about Pong?

450
00:31:30,040 --> 00:31:31,360
Pong will work under Ramil.

451
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:36,600
Ramil has full authority
over this entire project.

452
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:44,760
Grandpa,

453
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:46,760
could you come to the office?

454
00:31:46,840 --> 00:31:48,080
What now?

455
00:31:51,080 --> 00:31:53,400
Chayanee's customers
were denied financing.

456
00:31:53,480 --> 00:31:55,360
They're asking for their deposits back.

457
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:05,640
Hello.

458
00:32:05,720 --> 00:32:07,840
I'm Pichai, the owner of this development.

459
00:32:07,920 --> 00:32:09,240
How can I help you?

460
00:32:09,320 --> 00:32:11,040
Your granddaughter

461
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:12,720
said anyone applying

462
00:32:12,800 --> 00:32:14,920
for financing here would be approved.

463
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:17,920
I paid the reservation deposit,
but the bank rejected my application.

464
00:32:19,480 --> 00:32:20,600
I'm sorry.

465
00:32:20,680 --> 00:32:24,160
There must have been some mistake.
I can contact another bank for you.

466
00:32:24,240 --> 00:32:25,280
No.

467
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:27,120
I want my deposit back.

468
00:32:27,200 --> 00:32:29,600
You promised full refunds
if financing was denied.

469
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:33,120
Pay me now, or I'll complain
to Consumer Protection

470
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:34,280
and take this all the way.

471
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:37,320
Of course. I'll refund
every customer in full.

472
00:32:38,280 --> 00:32:39,120
Hathaya,

473
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:41,720
take them to process their refunds.

474
00:32:42,320 --> 00:32:43,360
Yes, Grandpa.

475
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:45,680
I apologize for the mistake.

476
00:32:46,280 --> 00:32:47,880
Don't make promises you can't keep.

477
00:32:50,440 --> 00:32:51,560
This way, please.

478
00:32:52,720 --> 00:32:53,600
This way.

479
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:55,840
Please have a seat.

480
00:32:59,800 --> 00:33:00,840
Grandpa,

481
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:03,080
I can contact other banks.

482
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:05,880
I'll find one that's willing
to approve their loans.

483
00:33:07,760 --> 00:33:10,480
Bring me the customers' reservation forms.

484
00:33:10,560 --> 00:33:11,600
Yes, sir.

485
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:25,400
HOME FOR SALE
FROM 4.8 MILLION BAHT

486
00:33:27,120 --> 00:33:28,040
What did they say?

487
00:33:28,120 --> 00:33:30,680
None of the financing applicants
were approved.

488
00:33:30,760 --> 00:33:32,240
We must refund all their deposits.

489
00:33:34,960 --> 00:33:36,160
Mr. Pichai must be furious.

490
00:33:46,200 --> 00:33:49,080
You raised the wages for Pong's crew.

491
00:33:50,160 --> 00:33:51,800
How can Ramil manage his workers now?

492
00:33:52,400 --> 00:33:54,480
Management needs one consistent standard.

493
00:33:56,520 --> 00:33:58,200
Father,

494
00:33:58,280 --> 00:34:00,280
we had to pay them more

495
00:34:00,360 --> 00:34:02,080
to get them back to work.

496
00:34:02,680 --> 00:34:03,640
And then what?

497
00:34:04,360 --> 00:34:05,880
You give them more once,

498
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:08,600
and the next time
they'll bargain for even more.

499
00:34:09,840 --> 00:34:13,000
You can call me stupid if you want,

500
00:34:13,080 --> 00:34:14,960
but everything Chayanee and I did

501
00:34:15,040 --> 00:34:17,320
was to make sure our project succeeded.

502
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:18,719
Was that really wrong?

503
00:34:19,880 --> 00:34:22,760
If you had done it correctly,
I wouldn't have said a word.

504
00:34:23,520 --> 00:34:25,880
If you don't know
how to manage people, then don't do it.

505
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:33,679
Grandpa, don't blame Mom.

506
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:37,480
I was the one who agreed
to Pong's proposal.

507
00:34:37,560 --> 00:34:38,800
It was my fault.

508
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:40,480
And you.

509
00:34:41,360 --> 00:34:43,120
I told you repeatedly that

510
00:34:43,679 --> 00:34:47,400
with the economy declining like this,
you must not use that promotion.

511
00:34:48,480 --> 00:34:51,560
But those customers
were referred by Uncle Saksit.

512
00:34:51,639 --> 00:34:54,159
I didn't think there would be a problem.

513
00:34:55,719 --> 00:34:57,400
When you run a business,

514
00:34:57,920 --> 00:34:59,760
you have to examine every angle.

515
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:02,000
You cannot operate based purely on trust.

516
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:09,280
Every one of those customers
has significant debt.

517
00:35:12,520 --> 00:35:15,880
Their incomes are unstable.

518
00:35:16,560 --> 00:35:18,600
Their existing debt levels
are already high.

519
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:21,920
More than 40 reservations
have now been canceled.

520
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:25,000
We have to start all over again
and find new customers.

521
00:35:25,080 --> 00:35:26,560
See how much damage this has caused?

522
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:29,880
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

523
00:35:29,960 --> 00:35:33,520
I promise this will never happen again.

524
00:35:35,080 --> 00:35:37,360
Instead of apologizing, you should study

525
00:35:37,440 --> 00:35:39,920
how other people think
and learn from their good ideas.

526
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:43,320
These are Hathaya's reservations.

527
00:35:45,720 --> 00:35:48,080
Her customers were approved
and paid in full.

528
00:35:53,040 --> 00:35:56,360
From now on,
Hathaya will be fully in charge of sales.

529
00:36:07,240 --> 00:36:08,640
I won't accept this, Mom.

530
00:36:09,920 --> 00:36:12,720
Hathaya already handles
the marketing plan,

531
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:16,760
helps check the accounts,
and now Father is giving her sales too.

532
00:36:16,840 --> 00:36:18,960
Ramil controls all the workers.

533
00:36:20,160 --> 00:36:22,240
Everything is in their hands.

534
00:36:23,320 --> 00:36:24,440
I won't accept it.

535
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:27,920
Sweetheart.

536
00:36:28,760 --> 00:36:31,120
Grandpa. Grandpa.

537
00:36:31,200 --> 00:36:35,040
You can't suddenly give someone
what belonged to Mom and me.

538
00:36:38,200 --> 00:36:41,440
The someone is also my granddaughter.

539
00:36:42,080 --> 00:36:43,880
But you said yourself

540
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:45,640
that you didn't trust Hathaya.

541
00:36:45,720 --> 00:36:48,480
You said she inherited
bad blood from her mother.

542
00:36:49,800 --> 00:36:50,800
Yes.

543
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:53,880
I said that because I misunderstood her.

544
00:36:54,960 --> 00:36:58,080
But Hathaya has proved herself now.

545
00:36:58,160 --> 00:36:59,920
She isn't like that.

546
00:37:00,720 --> 00:37:02,080
I understand that now.

547
00:37:02,600 --> 00:37:06,160
And I refuse to be an old man who
carries prejudice until the day he dies.

548
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:08,080
I have to make this right.

549
00:37:10,800 --> 00:37:14,040
I'm going to let Hathaya
manage this project.

550
00:37:15,680 --> 00:37:16,960
Chayanee,

551
00:37:17,040 --> 00:37:20,240
calm down. Get a hold of yourself.
We need to figure out what to do.

552
00:37:20,320 --> 00:37:22,800
No, Mom, I won't accept this.

553
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:24,240
Grandpa.

554
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:26,520
Careful. Grandpa could fall.

555
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:35,720
Grandpa. Grandpa.

556
00:37:36,360 --> 00:37:38,720
You can't give my work to someone else.

557
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:39,920
I won't accept it.

558
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:42,560
I've made my decision.

559
00:37:42,640 --> 00:37:45,680
Grandpa, give me another chance.

560
00:37:45,760 --> 00:37:47,680
Give your favorite granddaughter
another chance.

561
00:37:50,240 --> 00:37:52,040
It's because I love you

562
00:37:52,920 --> 00:37:56,000
that I've given in to you again and again.

563
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:59,640
From now on, if you want me to trust you,

564
00:37:59,720 --> 00:38:01,280
start a new business

565
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:03,320
and prove to me that you can succeed.

566
00:38:06,640 --> 00:38:09,440
No. I want to manage this project.

567
00:38:09,520 --> 00:38:12,400
I won't let anyone
take what belongs to me.

568
00:38:12,480 --> 00:38:14,040
I won't accept it, Grandpa.

569
00:38:14,840 --> 00:38:16,880
Chaya!

570
00:38:20,920 --> 00:38:21,920
Sir!

571
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:27,880
Grandpa.

572
00:38:33,480 --> 00:38:35,040
Grandpa. Are you hurt?

573
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:18,960
You can leave Grandpa here.

574
00:39:19,040 --> 00:39:21,920
Chayanee and I will take care of him.

575
00:39:22,960 --> 00:39:24,440
Father,

576
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:27,160
I prepared a room for you downstairs,

577
00:39:27,240 --> 00:39:29,640
so you won't have to keep
going up and down the stairs.

578
00:39:29,720 --> 00:39:34,000
Chayanee, help Grandpa
to his room. Come on.

579
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:35,640
I don't need either of you.

580
00:39:45,520 --> 00:39:46,760
Grandpa,

581
00:39:47,760 --> 00:39:50,320
I know you're angry with me.

582
00:39:52,160 --> 00:39:54,640
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to do it.

583
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:58,800
I'm truly sorry, Grandpa.

584
00:40:00,280 --> 00:40:02,600
I don't know what else I can do

585
00:40:02,680 --> 00:40:04,600
to make you forgive me.

586
00:40:10,800 --> 00:40:13,680
You have to accept Hathaya
moving back into this house.

587
00:40:20,600 --> 00:40:22,800
You were the one who asked me

588
00:40:23,640 --> 00:40:25,680
to make Hathaya live somewhere else.

589
00:40:27,240 --> 00:40:29,280
I agreed because you asked me to.

590
00:40:30,080 --> 00:40:32,640
You promised you would change.

591
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:35,840
But you couldn't keep that promise.

592
00:40:37,680 --> 00:40:40,280
As far as I'm concerned,
your request is no longer valid.

593
00:40:47,880 --> 00:40:48,760
Hathaya.

594
00:40:52,880 --> 00:40:54,080
Yes, Grandpa.

595
00:40:55,680 --> 00:40:58,120
While I'm recovering,

596
00:40:59,200 --> 00:41:02,400
move back in here. Help take care of me.

597
00:41:07,320 --> 00:41:09,720
And help manage the development.

598
00:41:21,040 --> 00:41:22,720
Thank you, Grandpa.

599
00:41:24,680 --> 00:41:26,400
I'll do everything I can.

600
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:29,600
Thank you so much.

601
00:41:31,800 --> 00:41:33,880
Ramil. Let's go.

602
00:42:06,800 --> 00:42:08,880
When I think about it,
I can't help laughing.

603
00:42:09,600 --> 00:42:11,880
Sometimes my life feels like
I'm constantly moving.

604
00:42:12,480 --> 00:42:14,720
Your life does sound interesting.

605
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:15,760
Quite an adventure.

606
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:18,920
But maybe

607
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:22,600
this will be your last move.

608
00:42:24,320 --> 00:42:27,520
I can tell Mr. Pichai
has finally opened his heart to you.

609
00:42:28,080 --> 00:42:30,080
He probably wants you to live there

610
00:42:30,600 --> 00:42:34,360
as his granddaughter.

611
00:42:36,720 --> 00:42:40,160
I want to be with Grandpa.
I want to take care of him.

612
00:42:41,920 --> 00:42:44,720
That's good. But…

613
00:42:47,120 --> 00:42:48,680
you need to be very careful.

614
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:51,120
Liu and Chayanee

615
00:42:51,640 --> 00:42:53,200
are extremely unhappy with you.

616
00:42:54,320 --> 00:42:57,520
But I've never tried
to take their inheritance.

617
00:42:57,600 --> 00:42:59,320
They don't think the way you do.

618
00:43:01,400 --> 00:43:04,960
If anything happens, tell me immediately.

619
00:43:08,160 --> 00:43:09,120
Let's go.

620
00:43:16,160 --> 00:43:17,680
Give me the bag.

621
00:43:19,080 --> 00:43:20,400
I'll take you over there.

622
00:43:20,480 --> 00:43:23,240
And we're going to pick up
someone important to you too.

623
00:43:26,440 --> 00:43:27,760
-Who?
-Come on.

624
00:43:30,680 --> 00:43:34,600
Ann, you don't need to bother.

625
00:43:34,680 --> 00:43:36,320
Don't try to stop me.

626
00:43:36,400 --> 00:43:39,200
Mr. Pichai ordered me to prepare
this room for Miss Hathaya.

627
00:43:40,560 --> 00:43:42,560
Listen to you calling her

628
00:43:42,640 --> 00:43:45,080
Miss Hathaya so proudly. Please.

629
00:43:45,160 --> 00:43:47,080
He's letting her stay here

630
00:43:47,160 --> 00:43:50,400
as a worker,
not as his beloved granddaughter.

631
00:43:51,000 --> 00:43:53,880
Is that so, Housekeeper Chamoi?

632
00:43:54,760 --> 00:43:57,800
Why are you acting so smug with me?

633
00:43:57,880 --> 00:44:00,840
You should use that tiny brain
of yours once in a while.

634
00:44:01,840 --> 00:44:05,280
If he didn't love and accept Miss Hathaya,

635
00:44:05,360 --> 00:44:07,880
do you really think
he would let her move back here?

636
00:44:07,960 --> 00:44:10,360
Think. Come on. Think.

637
00:44:11,080 --> 00:44:14,320
Before long, your bosses

638
00:44:14,400 --> 00:44:18,360
might be the one who gets pushed aside.

639
00:44:18,440 --> 00:44:20,680
That was harsh.

640
00:44:20,760 --> 00:44:23,200
You do not get to insult
my madam and Miss Chayanee.

641
00:44:23,800 --> 00:44:25,720
I warned you before.

642
00:44:26,440 --> 00:44:29,400
Everything can change.

643
00:44:29,480 --> 00:44:33,760
Madam and Miss Chayanee
used to rule this house.

644
00:44:34,720 --> 00:44:36,680
But before long,

645
00:44:38,600 --> 00:44:40,920
you may be the one in trouble.

646
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:43,760
Don't threaten me. I'm not scared.

647
00:44:43,840 --> 00:44:46,000
My madam

648
00:44:46,080 --> 00:44:47,960
will always protect me.

649
00:44:48,040 --> 00:44:49,640
The real question is

650
00:44:49,720 --> 00:44:51,680
how long Hathaya will last here.

651
00:44:51,760 --> 00:44:54,360
She'll probably get thrown out
again just like last time.

652
00:44:54,440 --> 00:44:55,280
Chamoi.

653
00:44:55,360 --> 00:44:57,360
I already told you

654
00:44:57,440 --> 00:44:59,080
not to act smug

655
00:44:59,160 --> 00:45:00,360
or raise your voice at me.

656
00:45:00,440 --> 00:45:01,520
Why not?

657
00:45:01,600 --> 00:45:02,960
We'll see

658
00:45:03,040 --> 00:45:05,760
who ends up

659
00:45:05,840 --> 00:45:08,240
running this house.

660
00:45:11,120 --> 00:45:12,000
Where are you going?

661
00:45:12,080 --> 00:45:13,640
Come back and finish this argument.

662
00:45:13,720 --> 00:45:15,840
It's annoying here.

663
00:45:15,920 --> 00:45:18,320
I'm going to welcome Miss Hathaya.

664
00:45:19,440 --> 00:45:21,880
Annoying? What's annoying?

665
00:45:21,960 --> 00:45:24,480
The sound of a dog barking.

666
00:45:26,120 --> 00:45:29,240
Hey. I'm not a dog!
If you've got the nerve, come back here.

667
00:45:35,720 --> 00:45:37,920
Here it is, Grandma. Grandpa's house.

668
00:45:39,080 --> 00:45:39,920
Hello,

669
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:42,560
Grandma Duangjai. Do you remember me?

670
00:45:43,720 --> 00:45:45,960
I'll be straight with you. No.

671
00:45:46,040 --> 00:45:47,080
I'm old.

672
00:45:47,160 --> 00:45:48,680
We met

673
00:45:48,760 --> 00:45:50,960
when Hathai first came to live here.

674
00:45:51,040 --> 00:45:52,360
Then we met again

675
00:45:52,440 --> 00:45:55,000
after she gave birth to Miss Hathaya.

676
00:45:56,680 --> 00:45:57,920
Now I remember.

677
00:45:58,560 --> 00:46:00,960
You were the one who helped raise Hathaya.

678
00:46:02,200 --> 00:46:03,440
That's right.

679
00:46:04,560 --> 00:46:06,560
Aunt Ann, I'm bringing her
to live here with me.

680
00:46:06,640 --> 00:46:08,000
Really?

681
00:46:08,080 --> 00:46:09,360
That's wonderful.

682
00:46:09,440 --> 00:46:11,400
I'll take very good care of her.

683
00:46:12,280 --> 00:46:13,400
Thank you.

684
00:46:13,480 --> 00:46:16,120
-Come in.
-Come on. Let's go, Grandma.

685
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:19,760
-I'll take the bags.
-Thanks.

686
00:46:19,840 --> 00:46:21,440
What is this?

687
00:46:22,440 --> 00:46:25,720
Father said you could move back in.

688
00:46:25,800 --> 00:46:27,640
Now you're bringing your relative too?

689
00:46:28,360 --> 00:46:30,560
Exactly, madam.

690
00:46:30,640 --> 00:46:33,200
Give someone an inch and they take a mile.

691
00:46:35,080 --> 00:46:36,760
You're Liu, right?

692
00:46:36,840 --> 00:46:38,080
Hello.

693
00:46:38,600 --> 00:46:40,520
You're still as beautiful as ever.

694
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:45,240
And you must be Chamoi. I remember you.

695
00:46:46,160 --> 00:46:48,600
Why? Because I'm still beautiful?

696
00:46:48,680 --> 00:46:50,400
Your mouth is still as nasty as ever.

697
00:46:54,480 --> 00:46:55,560
Mom,

698
00:46:56,400 --> 00:46:59,160
Hathaya probably isn't bringing
Grandma here to live.

699
00:46:59,240 --> 00:47:02,040
She's probably just
dropping her off. Hathaya,

700
00:47:02,120 --> 00:47:05,320
now that you're here, she can go home.

701
00:47:18,920 --> 00:47:20,120
Hathaya.

702
00:47:20,200 --> 00:47:21,520
Bring your grandma back out here.

703
00:47:21,600 --> 00:47:22,960
I said come back out.

704
00:47:23,040 --> 00:47:23,960
Mom.

705
00:47:24,040 --> 00:47:25,600
She's openly challenging us now.

706
00:47:26,120 --> 00:47:27,280
She's gone too far.

707
00:47:28,480 --> 00:47:29,360
Come on.

708
00:47:30,680 --> 00:47:31,600
Wait.

709
00:47:31,680 --> 00:47:34,320
Put those bags down, Ann.

710
00:47:34,400 --> 00:47:35,520
Chamoi.

711
00:47:35,600 --> 00:47:37,560
What?

712
00:47:37,640 --> 00:47:39,040
Hathaya.

713
00:47:39,120 --> 00:47:40,520
Hathaya. Didn't you hear me?

714
00:47:40,600 --> 00:47:42,600
Take your grandmother back home.

715
00:47:44,960 --> 00:47:47,520
I'm the one who told Hathaya
to bring her grandmother here.

716
00:47:49,280 --> 00:47:50,760
Hello, sir.

717
00:47:51,360 --> 00:47:53,840
Thank you so much

718
00:47:53,920 --> 00:47:56,960
for paying for my hospital treatment

719
00:47:57,040 --> 00:48:00,080
and for being kind enough
to let me stay here too.

720
00:48:00,680 --> 00:48:02,040
There's no need to be formal.

721
00:48:02,920 --> 00:48:04,600
You're practically family to me.

722
00:48:05,720 --> 00:48:06,760
Father,

723
00:48:07,280 --> 00:48:10,400
why did you have Hathaya
bring her grandmother here too?

724
00:48:10,480 --> 00:48:12,200
Exactly, Grandpa.

725
00:48:12,280 --> 00:48:14,640
Hathaya alone is already
enough of a burden.

726
00:48:16,920 --> 00:48:20,040
Hathaya helps me
with a great deal of work here.

727
00:48:20,680 --> 00:48:21,680
And she does it well.

728
00:48:23,800 --> 00:48:27,960
If you think Hathaya is a burden,

729
00:48:28,840 --> 00:48:32,880
then perhaps you should think carefully
about who the real burdens are.

730
00:48:39,360 --> 00:48:40,720
Hathaya,

731
00:48:40,800 --> 00:48:43,560
your grandmother has traveled
a long way. She must be tired.

732
00:48:44,080 --> 00:48:45,600
Take her to rest.

733
00:48:47,960 --> 00:48:49,800
Yes, Grandpa. Excuse us.

734
00:48:56,120 --> 00:48:57,680
I'd like to go rest too.

735
00:48:57,760 --> 00:48:59,720
Go help Grandpa.

736
00:48:59,800 --> 00:49:01,240
Ramil, take me.

737
00:49:04,480 --> 00:49:05,520
Yes, sir.

738
00:49:12,880 --> 00:49:13,960
Mom.

739
00:49:14,640 --> 00:49:16,320
I hate her.

740
00:49:17,360 --> 00:49:19,000
Today she brought her grandmother here.

741
00:49:19,720 --> 00:49:22,720
Next thing you know,
she'll bring her mother here to live too.

742
00:49:22,800 --> 00:49:25,800
Chayanee, don't let Grandpa
hear you say that.

743
00:49:25,880 --> 00:49:27,800
We'll be in trouble.

744
00:49:28,400 --> 00:49:30,360
For now, just watch them.

745
00:49:30,440 --> 00:49:32,280
We'll deal with them later.

746
00:49:37,760 --> 00:49:41,720
Where are you rushing off to? Your husband
said you give a great massage.

747
00:49:41,800 --> 00:49:43,760
But you were rude to me first.

748
00:49:43,840 --> 00:49:45,800
How could you put up with that?

749
00:49:46,400 --> 00:49:49,680
As long as I have a roof
over my head, that's enough.

750
00:49:49,760 --> 00:49:52,760
And as long as I get to be
with my granddaughter,

751
00:49:53,400 --> 00:49:54,520
I could even live under a bridge.

752
00:49:54,600 --> 00:49:56,560
-Grandma.
-Mom.

753
00:49:57,120 --> 00:49:59,040
-Grandma.
-Mom.

754
00:49:59,120 --> 00:50:01,040
NEXT EPISODE

755
00:51:59,400 --> 00:52:04,600
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
